title: Warpline M2 trust-floor bundle — closes v2-chain findings; v1 prefix still forgeable (corrected)
summary: 'CORRECTION to the initial "byte-authenticated end to end" claim: an adversarial Judge re-review + coordinator live exploits found the v1 half of the ledger is still forgeable. Built + verified the 4-item bundle (verified reads, merge-recipe presence check, grandfather body-pinning, lock owner-token + rewrite CAS), 263/263 tests, and it DOES defeat single-artifact hash-preserving tamper of v2 strands. But it does NOT authenticate v1 strand bindings (HIGH-A, T-2026-07-02-003: injected binding onto v1 seq 8 → verify exit 0 → restore materialized attacker files — REPRODUCED) nor make the legacy manifest tamper-proof (HIGH-B, T-2026-07-02-004: strand+manifest co-tamper of grandfathered seq 1 → verify "all intact" exit 0 — REPRODUCED). Root cause: the v1 prefix is anchored only at its tip (first v2 parentPickId); interior v1 bodies+bindings are malleable. Honest claim: v2 chain trustworthy; v1 prefix tamper-evident ONLY against single-file hash-preserving tamper.'
