body: 'Closes audit findings HIGH-2 (grandfather allowlist), HIGH-3/T-031 (ignore semantics), MEDIUM-1 (byte authenticity on read), MEDIUM-2 (rewrite guard bypass), and Judge''s net-new lock-ownership + CAS-less-rewrite finding. HIGH-1 (unsigned attribution) stays deferred to M3 by design — the docs (Move 0) no longer overclaim it. Commits on warpline-surfaces (pushed, 095256a1): 69652088 (item1) 1910080a (item2) 355b5343 (item3) 28687f0c (item4). Built by a worktree builder off warpline-surfaces; the 4 substantive commits were cherry-picked (dropping the builder''s .paradigm history-chore commit) and re-verified in the main checkout — 263/263, not trusting the subagent''s green. The OQ-D resolution + §7 legacy supersession are a dated amendment in docs/specs/warpline-fabric-schema-v2.md. Design calls: verified reads always-on (no opt-in); retired bare-string legacy manifest fails closed (regenerate error, no auto-upgrade — an unpinned grandfather clause is the hole); .warplineignore replaces rather than merges .gitignore; ignore v1 scope = root-level only. Follow-ups filed: T-2026-07-02-001 (freeze a hermetic fixture fabric — 2 migration tests read the live gitignored .warpline), T-2026-07-02-002 (Guard precision — ground-truth the 17 base-rate hits + rank direct-contested above closure ripple). This clears the PR-B precondition (verify now re-derives merge recipes) but PR-B stays evidence-gated on dogfooding actually hitting the H1 guard.'
